        "id": "E3",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "NVIDIA Mission Control 2.5 extends its autonomous recovery engine to Kubernetes-based workloads managed by NVIDIA Run:ai.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/how-nvidia-mission-control-2-5-brings-autonomous-recovery-to-kubernetes/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-26T15:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-29T01:46:31.349Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E4",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "The engine operates as a three-layer control loop: the Kubernetes scheduler places workloads, the autonomous job recovery service classifies failures using job context, and the autonomous hardware recovery service isolates and diagnoses faulty infrastructure.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/how-nvidia-mission-control-2-5-brings-autonomous-recovery-to-kubernetes/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-26T15:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-29T01:46:31.349Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E5",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Visit the documentation hub to learn how to upgrade to Mission Control 2.5.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/how-nvidia-mission-control-2-5-brings-autonomous-recovery-to-kubernetes/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
